          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#isometries Isometries
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry+group"} isometry group
            of Minkowski space is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentzian+geometry"} Lorentzian geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+of+special+relativity"} theory of special relativity
          %h3#gravitational_stability Gravitational stability
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Minkowski spacetimes is a
              %span.newWikiWord
                stable
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/gravitational+stability"} ?
              solution of the vacuum
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#ChristodoulouKlainerman"}> ChristodoulouKlainerman 1993
            ).
          %div
            %h3#HodgeStarOperatorOnMinkowskiSpacetime Hodge star operator on Minkowski spacetime
            %p
              We spell out component expressions for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+star+operator"} Hodge star operator
              on
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = d+1
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %h4#conventions Conventions
            %p
              We use
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+summation+convention"} Einstein summation convention
              throughout. With this convention, a generic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+p-form"} differential p-form
              reads
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi p
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha
                    \\;=\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{p!}
                    \\alpha_{ \color{green} \mu_1 \cdots \mu_p }
                    d x^{ \color{green} \mu_1}
                    \\wedge
                    \\cdots
                    \\wedge
                    d x^{\color{green} \mu_p}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo !
                    %mo ≔
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 3
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p! \coloneqq 1 \cdot 2 \cdot 3 \cdots p \,\in \mathbb{N} \subset \mathbb{R}
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorial"} factorial
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in \mathbb{N}
            %p
              We take the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+metric"} Minkowski metric
              to be the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \times D
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+matrix"} diagonal matrix
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi diag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta
                    \\;=\;
                    (\eta_{\mu \nu})
                    \\;=\;
                    (\eta^{\mu \nu})
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    diag(-1,+1, +1 , \cdots , +1)
                    \\,.
            %p
              We normalize the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+symbol"} Levi-Civita symbol
              as
            #eq:LCSymbolDown.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mi d
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon_{0 1 2 \cdots d}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    + 1
            %p which means that
            #eq:LCSymbolUp.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mi d
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon^{0 1 2 \cdots d}
                    \\;=\;
                    \- 1
                    \\,.
            %p
              We normalize the sign of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
              as
            #eq:VolumeForm.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi dvol
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mn 0
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mi d
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mrow
                                  %mi D
                                  %mo !
                            %msub
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mn 1
                                %mi ⋯
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi D
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mn 1
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ∧
                            %mi d
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    dvol
                    \&amp; \coloneqq\;
                    d x^0 \wedge d x^1 \wedge \cdots \wedge d x^d
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\tfrac{1}{D!}
                    \\epsilon_{
                    \\color{green}
                    \\mu_1 \cdots \mu_D
                    }
                    d x^{\color{green}\mu_1}
                    \\wedge
                    \\cdots
                    \\wedge
                    d x^{\color{green}\mu_D}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p We write
            #eq:GeneralizedKroneckerDelta.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi sgn
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo ∃
                                %mrow
                                  %mi σ
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi Sym
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %munder
                                  %mo ∀
                                  %mrow
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mo ≤
                                    %mi i
                                    %mo ≤
                                    %mi p
                                %mrow
                                  %mo (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ν
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi σ
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mi i
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo =
                                  %msub
                                    %mi μ
                                    %mi i
                                  %mo )
                                %mo )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mtext otherwise
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta^{ \mu_1 \cdots \mu_p }_{ \nu_1 \cdots \nu_p }
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    sgn(\sigma)
                    \&amp;\vert&amp;
                    \\underset{ \sigma \in Sym(p) }{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{1 \leq i \leq p}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    \\nu_{\sigma(i)} = \mu_i
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise}
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              for the generalized
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker+delta"} Kronecker delta
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+permutation"} signature
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
              that takes the upper indices to the lower indices, if any such exists, and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
              otherwise.
            %p
              This appears whenever the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Levi-Civita+symbol"} Levi-Civita symbol
              is contracted with itself:
            #eq:ContractionofLeviCivitaSymbols.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi p
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "blue"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "orange"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ν
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi ν
                            %mi p
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "blue"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathcolor => "magenta"}
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo −
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi p
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "orange"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon_{
                    { \color{green} \mu_1 \cdots \mu_p }
                    {\color{blue} \mu_{p+1} \cdots \mu_{D} }
                    }
                    \\epsilon^{
                    { \color{orange} \nu_1 \cdots \nu_p }
                    { \color{blue} \mu_{p+1} \cdots \mu_D }
                    }
                    \\;=\;
                    { \color{magenta} - }
                    (D-p)!
                    \\;
                    \\delta_{
                    \\color{green} \mu_1 \cdots \mu_p
                    }^{
                    \\color{orange} \nu_1 \cdots \nu_p
                    }
            %p
              Notice the minus sign in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ContractionofLeviCivitaSymbols"} (5)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LCSymbolUp"} (2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+quadratic+form"} signature
            %h4#definition Definition
            %p
              We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_\mu
              for the operator of contraction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d/d x^\mu
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anticommutator"} anticommutator
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi μ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi ν
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi μ
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big\{
                    \\iota_\mu, d x^\nu \wedge
                    \\big\}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\delta_\mu^\nu
            %p
              With the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
              as in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:VolumeForm"} (3)
              it follows that (notice the reversion of the index ordering in the contraction operators
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ι
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota
            #eq:ContractionIntoVolumeForm.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi α
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi p
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mn 1
                    %mi dvol
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi p
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "orange"}
                          %msub
                            %mi ν
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi ν
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi D
                              %mo −
                              %mi p
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "orange"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mstyle{:mathcolor => "orange"}
                        %msub
                          %mi ν
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi D
                            %mo −
                            %mi p
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha^{
                    \\color{green}
                    \\mu_1 \cdots \mu_p
                    }
                    \\iota_{\color{green} \mu_p}
                    \\cdots
                    \\iota_{ \color{green} \mu_1}
                    dvol
                    \\;=\;
                    \\epsilon_{
                    { \color{green} \mu_1 \cdots \mu_p }
                    { \color{orange} \nu_1 \cdots \nu_{(D-p)}  }
                    }
                    d x^{\color{orange} \nu_1}
                    \\wedge
                    \\cdots
                    \\wedge
                    d x^{\color{orange} \nu_{(D-p)}}
            .num_defn
              %h6#definition_2 Definition
              %p
                For a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+p-form"} differential p-form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                            %mi p
                            %mo !
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi p
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mn 1
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                          %msub
                            %mi μ
                            %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\alpha
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\tfrac{1}{ \color{green} p! }
                      \\alpha_{ \color{green} \mu_1 \cdots \mu_p}
                      d x^{ \color{green} \mu_1 }
                      \\wedge \cdots \wedge
                      d x^{ \color{green} \mu_p }
              %p
                its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+dual"} Hodge dual
                is:
              #eq:HodgeStar.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⋆
                              %mi α
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≔
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mrow
                                    %mstyle{:mathcolor => "green"}
                                      %mi p
                                      %mo !
                                    %mstyle{:mathcolor => "orange"}
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
